---
description: Keep one URL per page, split route groups by area, and vary features by role inside the page
alwaysApply: true
---

# Routes

`app/routes.ts` only composes groups. Each area owns one group file under `app/routing/`. Route modules under `app/routes/` stay thin: title and the feature page.

```
app/routes.ts
app/routing/public.routes.ts
app/routing/auth.routes.ts
app/routing/onboarding.routes.ts
app/routing/app.routes.ts
app/routes/orders.tsx          URL entry only
```

```ts
export default [
  ...publicRoutes,
  ...authRoutes,
  ...onboardingRoutes,
  ...appRoutes,
] satisfies RouteConfig;
```

Register each URL once. Add a new area as a new group file. Do not copy a page into a separate tree per role.

## Who can open the URL

A layout calls `requireAuth` or `requireRoles`. Roles missing from that list never get the page.

```ts
layout('shell/app/AppLayout.tsx', [
  route('dashboard', 'routes/dashboard.tsx'),
  route('settings', 'routes/settings.tsx'),
  layout('shell/app/StaffLayout.tsx', [
    route('orders', 'routes/orders.tsx'),
  ]),
]);
```

`StaffLayout` calls `requireRoles([Role.PHARMACY, Role.PROVIDER])`. Patient and admin are redirected. Pharmacy and provider share `/orders`.

Put the gate on the smallest layout that shares those roles. One role-only page can use its own layout. Do not check roles inside `app/routes/` modules.

## What that role sees

The feature page reads the role and renders only what that role can do. Same URL, different UI.

```ts
export function canCancelOrder(role: AppRole) {
  return role === 'pharmacy';
}
```

```tsx
{canCancelOrder(role) ? <CancelOrderButton /> : null}
```

Keep `canX(role)` next to the feature (`constants.ts` or `utils.ts`). Settings already does this with `settingsTabsFor`. Sidebar links come from `getAppNavGroups`. A missing nav item is not the gate — the layout still blocks the URL.

## Do not

```ts
// ❌ separate route trees that repeat /orders
export const pharmacyRoutes = [route('orders', 'routes/pharmacy/orders.tsx')];
export const providerRoutes = [route('orders', 'routes/provider/orders.tsx')];
```

```tsx
// ❌ role switch inside the route module
export default function Orders() {
  return role === 'pharmacy' ? <PharmacyOrdersPage /> : <ProviderOrdersPage />;
}
```
